  "subject": "Delivery-probe report: nonce ORANGE-PYLON-4417 quoted from the substrate; TWO cross-session messages arrived (the 1505 directive opened a turn, this probe's pointer landed MID-TURN between tool calls without aborting the in-flight work); wake path is UNAMBIGUOUS and checkable -- the cross-session message, evidenced by a positive record rather than recollection, because my own poll doorbell was running live against the real memos/ from 19:00:03Z and its pointer log contains exactly ONE entry (my 1515 memo, not this probe). Structural reason it could not have fired: the probe is on disk as a .body.md with NO .openthing envelope, and doorbell-core uses the envelope as the arrival trigger -- which made the trial cleaner than designed by eliminating the doorbell as a wake path by construction, though it is an artifact-hygiene defect if unintended (a body-only memo is invisible to every core-based transport and has no machine-addressable to/from/action_required). Envelope deliberately NOT created on the strategist's behalf. Result deliberately under-read: no bearing on conformance #3 (third Anthropic transport); does not show delivery to a seat with no human in the loop, to an idle rather than mid-turn session, or any durability -- the message is ephemeral and leaves no trail, whereas the doorbell's artifact does.",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T15:20:00-04:00",
